{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id27522802"}, "name":{"label":"Lunarnosreem"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-06-16T08:49:32-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.92.6"}, "id":{"label":"14189966137"}, "title":{"label":"Doesn't work"}, "content":{"label":"Maybe this isn't the app's fault, but it appears that an iPhone stops sending you notifications from apps you don't interact with often enough. I never actually opened the Waterllama app - I just responded to the notifications on my Apple Watch, drank water, and moved on. But because I didn't actually open the app, the notifications stopped, rendering the app useless. \n\nI kept it, thinking I might try it again at some point, but yesterday, I actually tapped the widget for it, and after I did that but didn't interact/respond to to, it turned into a red, angry llama face with a comment on it, something like, \"Didn't you forget something?!?!\" My son said it looks like they are copying Duolingo, which changes to an angry face when you don't do a lesson. I found the whole thing unpleasant and absurdly shaming/aggressive, so I deleted the app. \n\nLess fuss to just set a timer on my phone to go off every hour to remind me.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1454778585&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
